    {
      "type": 1,
      "name": "DiagnosisHeading",
      "content": {
        "json": "## Throttling diagnosis \u2014 disk limit or VM SKU limit?\n\nThese charts show the **peak consumed percentage** (Maximum) over the selected time range for the selected VM. A line reaching ~100% means that ceiling was hit.\n\n* **A DISK chart reaches ~100%** \u2192 an individual data disk hit its own provisioned IOPS or bandwidth limit \u2192 resize or upgrade that disk. Each line is one LUN, so you can see which disk.\n* **A VM SKU chart reaches ~100%** \u2192 the VM hit its aggregate IOPS or bandwidth limit across all disks \u2192 resize the VM.\n* **Both high** \u2192 the disk is saturating and rolling up to the VM limit too.\n\nUse the detailed trend charts below for per-LUN latency and cached/uncached breakdowns.\n\n_These charts show the peak over the selected time range \u2014 the worst moment, not the current state. Narrow the time range to see current activity._"
      }
    },
