    {
      "type": 1,
      "name": "VmSkuLimits",
      "content": {
        "json": "### VM SKU maximum limits \u2014 {VmSkuSize}\n\nThe absolute IOPS and throughput ceilings are set by this VM SKU (**{VmSkuSize}**) and change when you select a different VM. Rather than fixed numbers, use the **VM cached and uncached consumed %** charts below: they measure the selected VM\u2019s live usage against its own SKU ceilings, so a series near 100% means the VM SKU aggregate limit is the bottleneck (resize the VM). The per-disk provisioned limits above show each attached disk\u2019s own ceiling.\n\n_Need the exact published numbers? Look up **{VmSkuSize}** in the Azure VM sizes documentation._"
      }
    },
